# Panel 244's R1, spec § 1 as it landed on 2026-11-11: the catalogue names a
# package "with its source, exact version and `sum`, or by a local `path`
# alone, which nothing verifies". This entry names the `path` alone: the
# program builds, is told on stderr that no fingerprint holds the folder, and
# prints 2.
#
# It is the second case of the spec-warden's P2 (i), registered in
# `docs/panel/244-reports/spec-warden.md` § 5 and scored at M-core-packages'
# close: falsified if it flips while the sentence stands. Its twin, an entry
# naming a `path` and a `version`, is refused, in
# `tests/golden/check/catalogue-a-path-entry-holding-a-version-is-refused.case/`.
use <mypkg>/lib

function main()
    print(lib.two().to_str())
